"""Walking module: split-belt treadmill walking and other locomotor adaptation, one row per stride (or per step when that
is what the authors share).

Defined with the first walking dataset (Gonzalez-Rubio2019_FrontHumNeurosci). Columns hold the authors' own per-stride
values. Per-leg columns are named by the leg's role in the split-belt phase (_fast, _slow) because split-belt datasets
report legs that way, and some never say which side was fast; fast_leg gives the side when it is known. Lengths are in
metres and times in seconds (converted from mm or ms where the authors used those, as each README states).
The asymmetry columns have fixed formulas, stated in each description; a dataset whose authors used a different formula
leaves the column empty rather than putting a different quantity under the same name. A dataset fills only the columns
its authors shared: for example a deposit that keeps only asymmetry measures leaves the per-leg columns empty.
The perturbation itself (the belt-speed ratio) is in the CORE columns pert_type, pert_value and pert_unit."""

